<title>ESTONIA: BALTIC 30 INDEX UP 0.32 PERCENT TO 103.11.</title>
<headline>BALTIC 30 INDEX UP 0.32 PERCENT TO 103.11.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic 30 index, the only pan-Baltic index which is compiled by the three leading business newspapers, rose by 0.32 percent on Thursday to take it to 103.11, Estonia's Aripaev said.</p>
<p>The Baltic 30 index covers the 10 leading stocks from the three Baltic stock markets and is compiled by Aripaev, Lithuania's Verslo Zinios and Latvia's Dienas Bizness.</p>
<p>The index started from 100 on May 19.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
